From: VyOS LS1046A CI <ci@vyos-ls1046a>
Date: Thu, 17 Jul 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman_pcd: restore CONT_LOOKUP scaffold as the always-active
 engage path (reverses 0161 guard)

0161 made the CONT_LOOKUP pass-through scaffold conditional on
fe_enter_off==0, adding an else-free "skip scaffold" path that causes
RCCB to point directly at FE_ENTER — bypassing the safe group-table
pass-through and entering the FE-VM, which (a) never achieved a HIT,
(b) caused BMI port stalls requiring cold-boot, and (c) was superseded
by the settled architecture (qdrant 2026-07-16: CONT_LOOKUP pass-through
is the only silicon-proven kernel-delivery mechanism at 7.37 Gbps).

Restore the unconditional scaffold (always overwrites fe_enter_off = gro)
so RCCB points at the safe group table.  The FE-VM chain remains dormant
for the future HIT path.

Architecture reference: CONT_LOOKUP pass-through per RM 8.7.4.1 with
numKeys=0 → miss-AD → PCD FQ → kernel RSS.  M2-gate proven: 7.37 Gbps,
0.16% CPU, zero QMan errors.

Signed-off-by: VyOS LS1046A CI <ci@vyos-ls1046a>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
@@ -2269,7 +2269,7 @@ static int __fman_pcd_fe_arm_engage(struct fman_pcd *pcd,
 	if (miss_fqid == 0)
 		miss_fqid = 0x200;
 
-	if (fe_enter_off == 0) {
+	{
 		struct muram_info *muram = fman_get_muram(pcd->fman);
 		unsigned long gro, mto, ato;
 		if (muram) {
